//? Title: Fuzzy c-means: actual alternating updates and graded similarity
//? Subtitle: A hand-checkable start, the original overlapping blobs, Iris and the limits of membership
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Fuzzy c-means fits Euclidean centers and gives each point a graded membership in
every cluster, with each row summing to one. Three one-dimensional points make
the weighted center update and constrained membership update checkable.
Actual native traces then preserve the original overlapping-blob example,
including its center and objective values. Four raw Iris measurements provide
a descriptive application with species excluded from fitting. Fixed-center
queries expose a limitation: a very distant point can have nearly uniform
memberships. Phase objectives, actual work and owned history distinguish the
mathematical updates from floating-point stopping and resource limits.
)

\toc

> Three points and one actual alternating step

Take points 0,5,10, two clusters and fuzzifier m=2. Supply initial membership
rows (0.8,0.2), (0.5,0.5), (0.2,0.8). The left cluster uses squared weights
0.64,0.25,0.04, whose sum is 0.93. Its weighted numerator is 1.65, giving center
55/31, approximately 1.77419. The other center is 255/31, approximately 8.22581.
The following diagram uses actual accumulated numerators and denominators;
its returned membership row at the middle point is (0.5,0.5) at displayed precision.
Initial centers are zero, as in the seeded API.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fcm_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/fuzzy_c_means.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const dm::algorithms::FuzzyCMeansMatrix x{{0},{5},{10}},u{{.8,.2},{.5,.5},{.2,.8}};
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::fuzzy_c_means_trace_from(x,u,2,1,0,48);
  const auto& f=t.frames.at(0);
  std::print("| cluster | actual numerator | actual denominator | updated center |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t j=0;j<2;++j)std::print("| {} | {:.8f} | {:.8f} | {:.8f} |\n",j,f.numerators[j][0],f.denominators[j],f.centers[j][0]);
  std::print("\n| point | updated u0 | updated u1 |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<x.size();++i)std::print("| {:.0f} | {:.8f} | {:.8f} |\n",x[i][0],f.membership[i][0],f.membership[i][1]);
  std::print("\nObjective: before {:.8f}; after centers {:.8f}; after memberships {:.8f}. Maximum change {:.8f}; seeded draws {}.\n",f.objective_before,f.objective_centers,f.objective_membership,f.max_change,t.work.initial_draws);
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(62,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=4;box.height=2.2;box.font_size=21;
  d.node("u",{0,0},"Incoming U\n0.8 / 0.2\n0.5 / 0.5\n0.2 / 0.8",box)
   .node("v",{5.7,0},std::format("Actual weighted centers\n{:.2f}/{:.2f} = {:.5f}\n{:.2f}/{:.2f} = {:.5f}",f.numerators[0][0],f.denominators[0],f.centers[0][0],f.numerators[1][0],f.denominators[1],f.centers[1][0]),box)
   .node("new",{11.4,0},std::format("Updated U at x=5\n{:.5f} / {:.5f}\nmax change {:.5f}",f.membership[1][0],f.membership[1][1],f.max_change),box)
   .edge("u","v","u squared").edge("v","new","distances")
   .text({5.7,2.8},"One performed step; captured actual sums and memberships",25)
   .text({5.7,-2.4},std::format("J: {:.3f} -> {:.3f} -> {:.3f}",f.objective_before,f.objective_centers,f.objective_membership),27)
   .save_svg("build/fcm_tiny.svg");
  if(t.result.iterations!=1||std::abs(f.membership[1][0]-.5)>1e-14)throw std::runtime_error("tiny update");
}
