\caption(The center block minimizes the objective for incoming memberships; the membership block then uses those centers. Values are read from one actual supplied-start iteration.)
\alttext(A three-stage native diagram shows initial memberships, weighted numerators divided by weight sums, and updated middle-point membership one half one half. Objective values are printed below.)

> Derive the two updates

For points x_i, centers v_j and membership rows u_i constrained to the simplex,

$$
J_m(U,V)=\sum_i\sum_j u_{ij}^{m}\|x_i-v_j\|^2,\qquad
u_{ij}\ge0,\quad\sum_j u_{ij}=1,\quad m>1.
$$
\alttext(The fuzzy objective sums squared point-center distances weighted by the mth power of simplex-constrained memberships.)

Hold U fixed. For a cluster with positive powered weight W_j, differentiating
with respect to v_j gives 2(W_j v_j-sum_i u_ij^m x_i)=0. Thus

$$
v_j=\frac{\sum_i u_{ij}^{m}x_i}{\sum_i u_{ij}^{m}}.
$$
\alttext(A center is the weighted mean of points, with weights equal to powered incoming memberships.)

Now hold centers fixed and suppose all distances d_ij are positive.
A row's Lagrangian is sum_j u_ij^m d_ij² plus lambda_i(sum_j u_ij-1).
Its stationarity equation makes u_ij proportional to d_ij^(-2/(m-1)).
Normalization yields

$$
u_{ij}
=\frac{d_{ij}^{-2/(m-1)}}{\sum_\ell d_{i\ell}^{-2/(m-1)}}
=\left[\sum_\ell\left(\frac{d_{ij}}{d_{i\ell}}\right)^{2/(m-1)}\right]^{-1}.
$$
\alttext(Positive-distance memberships are normalized inverse powers of distances, equivalently reciprocals of sums of distance-ratio powers.)

For positive distances the row problem is strictly convex, so this is its unique
minimizer. Zero-distance centers require a separate choice supported on those
centers. The native policy assigns the whole row to the last center whose
computed distance is strictly below 1e-12. Several exactly coincident centers
could mathematically share weight; this implementation chooses one.
An all-zero incoming membership column leaves its old center unchanged.

Exact coordinate minimization cannot increase J. This is a block-descent
argument, not a global-optimum or finite-precision convergence certificate.
The near-coincidence threshold is approximate, floating operations round, and
the stopping test only checks the largest membership change against a tolerance.

[Dunn's 1973 paper](https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/abs/10.1080/01969727308546046)
introduced the fuzzy relative of ISODATA.
[Bezdek, Ehrlich and Full (1984)](https://doi.org/10.1016/0098-3004(84)90020-7)
give the objective and alternating updates in equations 11 and algorithm A1–A4,
printed pages 193–194
([full paper](https://web-ext.u-aizu.ac.jp/course/bmclass/documents/FCM%20-%20The%20Fuzzy%20c-Means%20Clustering%20Algorithm.pdf)).
Their discussion distinguishes membership from statistical uncertainty and allows
other norms. This native implementation uses Euclidean distance and its stated
near-coincidence policy.

> Preserve the original overlapping blobs

The original 160 one-dimensional points come from 80 Gaussian draws around 0 and 80
around 10, each with standard deviation 2.2, using mt19937_64 seed 21.
The library now owns that fixture and the query-membership calculation; the
report no longer duplicates either algorithm. Initialization uses seed 1 for the
fit, m=2, maximum 200 iterations and tolerance 1e-6. Standard-library distribution
mapping limits bit portability across implementations.

The trace records the two phase objectives from each actual iteration. Returned
centers were computed from the incoming memberships of the last iteration;
returned memberships were updated using those centers. There is no extra final
center update. The reported objective uses that exact returned pair.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fcm_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/fuzzy_c_means.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto data=dm::algorithms::fuzzy_c_means_example_data();
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::fuzzy_c_means_trace(data,2,2,200,1e-6,1);
  const auto& fit=t.result;const std::size_t left=fit.centers[0][0]<fit.centers[1][0]?0:1;
  std::print("Original blobs: {} points; {} iterations; objective {:.3f}; centers {:.7f}, {:.4f}; stopped by tolerance {}.\n",data.size(),fit.iterations,fit.objective,fit.centers[0][0],fit.centers[1][0],t.stopped_by_tolerance);
  const dm::algorithms::FuzzyCMeansMatrix queries{{0},{2.5},{5},{7.5},{10}};
  const auto membership=dm::algorithms::fuzzy_c_means_membership(queries,fit.centers);
  std::print("\n| query x | membership in left cluster |\n| ---: | ---: |\n");for(std::size_t i=0;i<queries.size();++i)std::print("| {:.1f} | {:.8f} |\n",queries[i][0],membership[i][left]);
  std::vector<double>xs,ys,phase{0},J{std::log10(t.initial_objective)};
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<data.size();++i){xs.push_back(data[i][0]);ys.push_back(fit.membership[i][left]);}
  std::print("\n| iteration | J after centers | J after memberships | maximum membership change |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(const auto& f:t.frames){std::print("| {} | {:.8f} | {:.8f} | {:.8f} |\n",f.iteration+1,f.objective_centers,f.objective_membership,f.max_change);phase.push_back(2*f.iteration+1);J.push_back(std::log10(f.objective_centers));phase.push_back(2*f.iteration+2);J.push_back(std::log10(f.objective_membership));}
  auto memberships=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  memberships.points(xs,ys,"Training rows",{37,99,235},3).abline_h(.5,{120,120,120},1).abline_v(fit.centers[left][0],{22,163,74},1).abline_v(fit.centers[1-left][0],{220,38,38},1)
   .title("Actual returned membership at each observed point").xlab("Position x").ylab("Membership in left cluster").y_limits(0,1.05);
  auto objective=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  objective.lines(phase,J,"",{220,38,38},2).points(phase,J,"",{220,38,38},3).title("One trace: both blocks, no optimization replay").xlab("Phase:0 initial, odd centers, even memberships").ylab("log10 of actual J");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(2,1).add(memberships).add(objective).size(1050,900).title("Original synthetic fixture; m=2, seed 1").fit_panels().save_svg("build/fcm_original.svg");
  if(fit.iterations!=11||std::abs(fit.objective-623.804)>5e-4)throw std::runtime_error("preserved original fit");
}
