\caption(The membership panel uses the actual returned rows. The lower panel plots the initial objective and both actual update phases per iteration; its logarithm is only a display transform.)
\alttext(Two native panels show graded left membership for the original 160 points and the descending log10 phase objectives over eleven iterations.)

The supplied prediction API also evaluates new points from fixed centers. Its
outputs are graded geometric similarities, not calibrated class probabilities
or estimates of how much mixture material generated an observation.

> Iris: four raw measurements, species held out of fitting

Use the canonical 150-row Iris table and all four numeric measurements in their
recorded centimetres. Species is excluded from the fit and appears only in
descriptive grouped means afterwards. No standardization is applied; changing
one coordinate's units changes Euclidean geometry. Cluster indices remain the
native fit order and can permute across seeds.

The coefficient F=(1/n)sum_ij u_ij² and entropy H=-(1/n)sum_ij u_ij log u_ij
describe concentration. Nominally 1/c<=F<=1 and 0<=H<=log c. They are not accuracy,
a calibrated uncertainty score, or automatic proof that c is appropriate.
Comparing their raw values across different c or m requires care.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fcm_iris.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/fuzzy_c_means.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  auto iris=dm::datasets::iris();
  const std::vector<std::string> features{"Sepal.Length","Sepal.Width","Petal.Length","Petal.Width"};
  dm::algorithms::FuzzyCMeansMatrix points(iris.nrows());
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<iris.nrows();++i)for(const auto& name:features)points[i].push_back(iris.double_at(name,i));
  const auto fit=dm::algorithms::fuzzy_c_means_work(points,3,2,300,1e-7,7);
  const auto part=dm::algorithms::fuzzy_c_means_partition(fit.result.membership);
  std::print("Iris: {} rows, four raw cm features; iterations {}; J {:.6f}; partition coefficient {:.6f}; entropy {:.6f} nats; stopped by tolerance {}.\n",points.size(),fit.result.iterations,fit.result.objective,part.coefficient,part.entropy_nats,fit.stopped_by_tolerance);
  std::print("\n| native cluster | Sepal.Length | Sepal.Width | Petal.Length | Petal.Width |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t j=0;j<3;++j){const auto& v=fit.result.centers[j];std::print("| {} | {:.6f} | {:.6f} | {:.6f} | {:.6f} |\n",j,v[0],v[1],v[2],v[3]);}
  std::vector<double>index,u0,u1,u2;
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<points.size();++i){index.push_back(i+1);u0.push_back(fit.result.membership[i][0]);u1.push_back(fit.result.membership[i][1]);u2.push_back(fit.result.membership[i][2]);}
  iris.add_column("u0",u0);iris.add_column("u1",u1);iris.add_column("u2",u2);
  const auto grouped=iris|dm::group_by("Species")|dm::summarise(dm::agg::mean("u0","mean_u0"),dm::agg::mean("u1","mean_u1"),dm::agg::mean("u2","mean_u2"));
  std::print("\nSpecies shown after fitting; descriptive membership means:\n{}\n",grouped.to_md());
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.lines(index,u0,"Cluster0",{37,99,235},1.5).lines(index,u1,"Cluster1",{220,38,38},1.5).lines(index,u2,"Cluster2",{22,163,74},1.5)
    .abline_v(50.5,{120,120,120},1).abline_v(100.5,{120,120,120},1)
    .legend({"Cluster0","Cluster1","Cluster2"},{{37,99,235},{220,38,38},{22,163,74}})
    .title("Iris memberships in canonical row order").xlab("Rows 1-50 setosa; 51-100 versicolor; 101-150 virginica").ylab("Graded membership, not species probability").y_limits(0,1.05).size(1100,540).save_svg("build/fcm_iris.svg");
  if(points.size()!=150||fit.result.centers.size()!=3||!std::isfinite(part.entropy_nats))throw std::runtime_error("Iris native fit");
}
