\caption(Changing m changes geometric softness at fixed centers. Both far tails approach one half, so fuzzy membership alone does not separate an outlier from an overlapping observation.)
\alttext(Four native curves peak at center zero, reach zero at center ten and return toward one half in both far tails. All curves cross one half at the midpoint.)

> Actual work, numerical domains and whole-history admission

Each performed center block costs order ncd; distance computation also costs
order ncd. This implementation uses the pairwise ratio formula directly,
so a noncoincident row evaluates c² ratio powers. Per iteration the combined
order is nc(d+c). A near-coincident row skips those ratio powers, while all
its distances were still computed. Input and result storage include nd,cd,nc;
the ordinary routine retains only its current state and scratch arrays.
Traced frames add retained history and extra phase objectives.

The trace quota counts matrix row records and scalar entries, not bytes or peak
RAM. With n points,d coordinates,c clusters and T requested iterations, its
whole upper bound is

$$
(2n+c+nd+nc+cd)+T(1+3c+2n+2cd+2nc).
$$
\alttext(Whole trace entries are two n plus c plus nd plus nc plus cd, then T times one plus three c plus two n plus two cd plus two nc.)

The base owns data, initial memberships and initial zero centers. Each frame
owns one metadata record, centers, memberships, actual numerators, denominators
and distances. The default cap is one million entries; zero disables only this
optional cap, while count and container bounds remain. Whole-request admission
precedes input copies and initialization draws, with no early-stop discount,
truncation or partial trace.

All shapes and finite values are checked before zero-iteration shortcuts and
quotas. Supplied membership rows must sum to one within absolute 1e-12 in
long-double accumulation and are not normalized. Actual nonfinite arithmetic
throws; an entirely underflowed positive cluster-weight column throws.
Individual finite rounding and underflow still require numerical judgment.
Trace phase objectives perform extra computations: an initial zero-center
objective can overflow even if an ordinary fitted final objective is representable.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fcm_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/fuzzy_c_means.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::algorithms::FuzzyCMeansMatrix x{{0},{5},{10}},u{{.8,.2},{.5,.5},{.2,.8}};
  bool rejected=false;try{(void)dm::algorithms::fuzzy_c_means_trace_from(x,u,2,1,0,47);}catch(const std::length_error&){rejected=true;}
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::fuzzy_c_means_trace_from(x,u,2,1,0,48);
  x[0][0]=99;u[0][0]=.1;const bool owned=t.data[0][0]==0&&t.initial_membership[0][0]==.8;
  const auto zero=dm::algorithms::fuzzy_c_means({{1},{3}},1,2,0);
  const auto tie=dm::algorithms::fuzzy_c_means_membership({{0}},{{0},{0}});
  bool ragged=false,nan=false,underflow=false;
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::fuzzy_c_means({{1,2},{3}},1,2,0);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){ragged=true;}
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::fuzzy_c_means({{NAN},{1}},1,2,0);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){nan=true;}
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::fuzzy_c_means({{1},{2}},2,10000,1);}catch(const std::underflow_error&){underflow=true;}
  std::print("Tiny upper entries {}; cap47 rejected {}; cap48 admitted true; owned after edits {}. Original upper entries {}.\n",dm::algorithms::fuzzy_c_means_trace_entries(3,1,2,1),rejected,owned,dm::algorithms::fuzzy_c_means_trace_entries(160,1,2,200));
  std::print("Zero iterations: center {}; memberships {}; J {}; iterations {}. Duplicate-center query membership {}.\n",zero.centers,zero.membership,zero.objective,zero.iterations,tie);
  std::print("Domain checks: ragged rejected {}; NaN rejected {}; all positive weights underflow rejected {}.\n",ragged,nan,underflow);
  std::print("\n| c | generic center weights | generic distances | generic ratio powers | coincident ratio powers |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  std::vector<double>cs,generic,coincident;
  dm::algorithms::FuzzyCMeansMatrix distinct,identical(24,std::vector<double>{0});for(int i=0;i<24;++i)distinct.push_back({double(i*i)});
  for(std::size_t c=1;c<=6;++c){
    const auto a=dm::algorithms::fuzzy_c_means_work(distinct,c,2,3,0,1);
    const auto b=dm::algorithms::fuzzy_c_means_work(identical,c,2,3,0,1);
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",c,a.work.center_weights,a.work.membership_distances,a.work.ratio_powers,b.work.ratio_powers);
    cs.push_back(c);generic.push_back(a.work.ratio_powers);coincident.push_back(b.work.ratio_powers);
  }
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.lines(cs,generic,"Distinct points",{37,99,235},2).points(cs,generic,"",{37,99,235},4)
    .lines(cs,coincident,"All coincident",{220,38,38},2).points(cs,coincident,"",{220,38,38},4)
    .legend({"Distinct points","All coincident"},{{37,99,235},{220,38,38}})
    .title("Actual ratio powers; n=24, d=1, three performed iterations").xlab("Requested clusters c").ylab("Executed pairwise ratio powers").size(1050,520).save_svg("build/fcm_controls.svg");
  if(!rejected||!owned||!ragged||!nan||!underflow)throw std::runtime_error("owned history and domain controls");
}
