\caption(The measured ratio-power cost grows quadratically in c for these distinct points. Coincident rows skip every ratio power after computing their distances. The entry-quota demonstration remains separate from executed operation counts.)
\alttext(Two native work curves compare ratio-power counts on24 distinct points and24 coincident points over three iterations. The distinct curve rises quadratically; coincident counts remain zero.)

A small final membership change is a stopping condition, not proof of the best
clustering or a semantic explanation of every ambiguous row. Keep the chosen
features, units, cluster count, fuzzifier, initialization, numerical limits and
interpretation of membership visible alongside the fit.
